    "reason": "The PR [ev-b1aec15857e6] says this change adds two opt-in options. They copy request or response headers onto client and server spans as attributes named `http.request.header.<key>` and `http.response.header.<key>`. So the change is an addition, and an operator who does nothing should see no effect. But none of the evidence names the two options or gives their configuration path. The changelog line [ev-7b4ea0fc44f3] doesn't, the PR description is cut off, and the changed-files list [ev-fdbf484ca131] only shows that the static config and the reference docs were edited. To write the subject and the applicability condition, we need the actual option keys and their place in the static configuration (for example, the docs/reference/static-configuration or pkg/config/static/static_config.go diff).",
